    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting an elite 81.88 efficiency score. His matchup against the shaky arm of Grayson Rodriguez (5.10 xERA) is our primary target, augmented by a favorable hitter's park and a powerful #3-hole spot. **Kyle Tucker** (73.84) and **Andy Pages** (68.24) also provide high-ceiling utility, with **Kyle Tucker** benefiting from a premium matchup against Assad and **Andy Pages** providing stable, high-efficiency production at the top of the order. We are leaning heavily into these right-handed bats against mid-tier arms to maximize our runs and RBI potential while maintaining our competitive advantage in the 5x5 standings.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Miguel Vargas** from the starting nine. While his 56.54 score was respectable and bolstered by strong underlying xwOBA metrics, the optimizer preferred the superior matchup context of **Denzer Guzman** (56.75) against the porous pitching of Povich. **Denzer Guzman** benefits from both a park factor bump and a platoon edge that ultimately squeezed him into the lineup ahead of **Miguel Vargas**. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Drake Baldwin**, whose 62.60 projection is impressive, but his status is clouded by a 44% rain risk in his matchup against Gusto; if that game is significantly delayed or washed out, it could force a late-day defensive adjustment to protect our remaining daily game caps.",
